# The Maps are not conditional on the destruction: Bot2 discards a card in response to make its Iron-Shield Elf indestructible
# (CR 702.12b), Get Lost's destroy does nothing, and Bot2 still creates two Map tokens (Get Lost's text and rulings: "its
# controller creates two Map tokens" whether or not it was destroyed).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Get Lost
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Iron-Shield Elf
Island
Swamp x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Iron-Shield Elf.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Get Lost.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Iron-Shield Elf)
Bot2.Battlefield.Iron-Shield Elf.Activate
Bot2.Choose(Island)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Swamp; Mox Jet; Iron-Shield Elf; Map Token; Map Token
Bot2.Battlefield.Iron-Shield Elf.Keywords = Indestructible
Bot2.Battlefield.Iron-Shield Elf.Tapped = true
Bot2.Graveyard = Island
